atment across the four flows so\n51\t  keyboard users can always identify the focused control.\n52\t- Keep the fixes scoped to keyboard operability: screen-reader semantics beyond\n53\t  what the keyboard fixes require, and flows outside the four audited ones, are\n54\t  out of scope per the strategy.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Given the project creation flow, When it is operated end to end with keyboard\n59\t  only, Then it completes with no focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n60\t- Given the workbench spawn flow, When it is operated end to end with keyboard\n61\t  only, Then it completes with no focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n62\t- Given the model deployment flow, When it is operated end to end with keyboard\n63\t  only, Then it completes with no focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n64\t- Given the pipeline run submission flow, When it is operated end to end with\n65\t  keyboard only, Then it completes with no focus traps and no unreachable\n66\t  controls.\n67\t- Every control reachable by pointer in the four audited flows is also\n68\t  reachable and activatable by keyboard.\n69\t- Visible focus indicators are present and visually consistent across all\n70\t  interactive controls in the four audited flows.\n71\t- Existing pointer-driven operation of the four flows is not regressed by the\n72\t  fixes.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- **HLR-1 (P1)** — The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard,\n77\t  with no focus traps or unreachable controls. Covered by this epic's\n78\t  remediation of all audit-enumerated defects across the four flows.\n79\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n80\t  flows. Covered by this epic's consistent focus-indicator treatment over the\n81\t  same four flows.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b956edc76ff10cd8","agent_id":"a13872cd13f94e9d4","session_id":"8d0ae72b-bef8-4903-b0b5-41dcee46a68e","uuid":"5f5101eb-e10d-43